# Single-output web build: there is one dist/index.html and every path must
# reach it, or a pasted link into an article or the archive is a host 404 —
# which is what made shared links dead on arrival.
#
# Committed here rather than set in the Netlify dashboard: `public/` is copied
# verbatim into `dist/`, which is the publish directory, so the rule ships with
# the build that needs it. Rebuild after editing this file — the export is what
# copies it.
#
# 200, not 301: the URL is preserved so the router can read it. No `!` — there
# is nothing to shadow in a single-output build, and forcing would only hide
# real asset 404s. Unmatched paths reach expo-router's own +not-found route.
/*    /index.html    200
